    (6, None, '\'You gave such a strange order yourself, Chef.\' English has one "order", Russian has two: "zakaz" is what you place in a restaurant, "prikaz" is a command. Fedya uses "prikaz". And "vy sami", "you yourself", is polite.'),
    (7, None, '\'Now it definitely cannot get any worse.\' It\'s the classic line that tempts fate. Russian says "worse already exactly to be cannot". "Khuzhe", "worse", is worth learning together with "luchshe", "better".'),
